  <main class="main" id="main-content">
    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-title">What is the Investor Personality Quiz?</h2>
      <p class="section-body">Choosing a stock portfolio allocation isn't just a math problem — it's also a behavioral one. Two investors with identical incomes can need very different portfolios depending on how they actually react to volatility, how long their time horizon really is, and what kind of decision-making style they have under stress. The Investor Personality Quiz captures this by asking about your age range, risk tolerance, and personality-style preferences, in a spirit similar to MBTI-style categorization.</p>
      <p class="section-body">Based on your answers, you're matched to one of 40 distinct portfolio archetypes, each with a suggested allocation across widely-used ETFs like QQQ (growth-oriented Nasdaq exposure), SPY (broad market exposure), and SCHD (dividend-focused stability). The result also explains the reasoning behind the match, not just the raw numbers.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Why Use This Tool?</h2>
      <p class="section-body">Many investors pick an allocation based on what's trending or what a friend recommended, then panic-sell during the first serious downturn because the portfolio never actually matched their real risk tolerance. This quiz is designed to surface that mismatch before it costs you money, by starting from your behavioral tendencies rather than just your stated goals.</p>
      <p class="section-body">It's also simply a fun, fast way to think concretely about your own investing style — the kind of self-reflection exercise that's easy to skip but genuinely useful before committing real capital.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-title">How to Take the Investor Personality Quiz</h2>
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li class="step-item">
          <span class="step-num">1</span>
          <div class="step-body"><strong class="step-name">Open the quiz</strong><p class="step-text">Click Open Tool below. The quiz begins immediately — no login or setup required.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li class="step-item">
          <span class="step-num">2</span>
          <div class="step-body"><strong class="step-name">Answer questions about yourself</strong><p class="step-text">Answer a short series of questions covering your age range, risk tolerance, and personality-style preferences (similar in spirit to MBTI categories).</p></div>
        </li>
        <li class="step-item">
          <span class="step-num">3</span>
          <div class="step-body"><strong class="step-name">Get your matched portfolio type</strong><p class="step-text">Based on your answers, the quiz matches you to one of 40 portfolio archetypes, each with a suggested allocation across ETFs like QQQ, SPY, and SCHD.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li class="step-item">
          <span class="step-num">4</span>
          <div class="step-body"><strong class="step-name">Review the reasoning behind the match</strong><p class="step-text">The result explains why that particular allocation fits your risk profile and behavioral tendencies, not just the raw percentages.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li class="step-item">
          <span class="step-num">5</span>
          <div class="step-body"><strong class="step-name">Use it as a conversation starter, not a final decision</strong><p class="step-text">Treat the result as a helpful starting point for thinking about your own asset allocation — not a substitute for your own research or professional financial advice.</p></div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
        <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
          <h3 class="faq-q" itemprop="name">What is the Investor Personality Quiz?</h3>
          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p class="faq-a" itemprop="text">It is a free 3-minute quiz that asks about your age, risk tolerance, and personality style, then matches you to one of 40 suggested US stock portfolio allocations built from ETFs like QQQ, SPY, and SCHD.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
          <h3 class="faq-q" itemprop="name">How long does the quiz take?</h3>
          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p class="faq-a" itemprop="text">Most people complete it in about 3 minutes. There is no account creation or personal data collection required.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
          <h3 class="faq-q" itemprop="name">Is the portfolio result personalized financial advice?</h3>
          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p class="faq-a" itemprop="text">No. The result is an educational starting point based on general investor archetypes, not individualized financial advice. Always consider your own full financial picture, or consult a licensed advisor, before making investment decisions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
          <h3 class="faq-q" itemprop="name">How many portfolio types are there?</h3>
          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p class="faq-a" itemprop="text">There are 40 distinct portfolio archetypes, generated from combinations of age range, risk tolerance, and personality-style categories similar in spirit to MBTI.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
          <h3 class="faq-q" itemprop="name">Do I need an account to take the quiz?</h3>
          <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p class="faq-a" itemprop="text">No. The Investor Personality Quiz is completely free and requires no sign-up, no account, and no personal information of any kind.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section related-section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Related Free Tools</h2>
      <div class="rel-grid">
